===Etymology===
Probably related to {{och-l|晦|dark}}; in numerous [[Zhou]] texts {{lang|zh|海}} is described as {{lang|zh|晦}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}). Compare the parallelism in Chinese: {{och-l|溟|ocean}} < {{och-l|冥|dark}}.

STEDT compares {{och-l|海}} to {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*muːŋ ~ r/s-muːk||foggy; dark; sullen; menacing; thunder}}, but the rhymes are incompatible.

Lai reconstructs a new cognate set connecting this word with {{cog|sit-bok|simu|t=lake}} and {{cog|jiq|rbó|t=pond}}. To cover these cognates, something like {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*m̥əq}} would have to be reconstructed.

