===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|うみ}}
{{wp|ja:}}
{{wp|Sea}}
{{wp|Ocean}}
{{IPAfont|⟨umi<sub>1</sub>⟩}} → *{{IPAchar|/umij/}} → {{IPAchar|/umi/}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}}, theorized as descending from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*omi}}.

Has been thought to have been derived from a compound. There are two leading theories regarding the ultimate derivation:
* Shift from {{m|ja|大|tr=ō-||[[big]], [[great]]}} + {{m|ja|水|tr=mi||[[water]]|pos=combining form}}.<ref>{{R:Nipponica}}</ref>
: This is problematic phonetically because there is no known term having a related shift from {{IPAchar|/opo/}} → {{IPAchar|/oː/}} → {{IPAchar|/o/}} → {{IPAchar|/u/}}, and semantically as there already exists a compound {{m|ja|大水|tr=ōmizu||[[flood]]}}.
* From {{m|ja|う|tr=u-|pos=stem indicating “[[ocean]]”}} + {{m|ja|水|tr=mi||water|pos=combining form}}. The ''u-'' stem is evident in {{m|ja|魚|tr=uo||[[fish]]}} and {{m|ja|潮|tr=ushio||[[salt water]]; [[tide]]}}, and in the {{m|ja|海|tr=una}} element in various ancient terms (see below).<ref>{{R:Gogen Yurai Jiten|海／うみ|umi}}</ref>

